ded includes the tiles BEFORE the meld is finalized**, but that doesn't fit.\n\nPerhaps the system allows temporary overlap for display.\n\nBut logically, after Chi B7 and forming [B6,B7,B8], the tiles B6 and B8 are gone from hand, B7 is added (from outside), so hand has: original 13 - B6 - B8 + B7.\n\nSo if original hand had B5\u00d72, B6, B7, B8, B9, etc., then after:\n- Remove B6, B8\n- Add B7\n\u2192 So B5\u00d72, B7 (original), B7 (new), B9 \u2192 B5\u00d72, B7\u00d72, B9\n\nBut in the list, B6 and B8 are still there \u2014 so inconsistency.\n\nGiven the data, I must trust the input as-is.\n\nPossibly, the \"hand tiles\" list includes all tiles you possess, and the meld is a subset.\n\nBut then total tiles exceed.\n\nAnother idea: perhaps the meld [B6,B7,B8] is formed, but the hand list shows what's left.\n\nBut B6, B7, B8 appear in both \u2014 impossible.\n\nUnless it's a mistake.\n\nLook at counts: B6:1 in hand, B7:1, B8:1 \u2014 and meld has one each \u2014 so total two B6, two B7, two B8? But unshown tiles show B6:3, B7:2, B8:3 \u2014 implying only 3 copies available, so cannot have duplicates.\n\nUnshown B6:3 \u2014 means 3 left in wall/unseen.\n\nTotal copies: 4.\n\nSo if unshown:3, then one is revealed (in some meld or discard).\n\nFrom histories:\n- Previous player: Play B7, B7, B4, B2, B1 \u2014 so discarded two B7s.\n- Next player: Play B4, B9\n- Across: Play B1, T2\n\nSo at least two B7 discarded.\n\nUnshown B7:2 \u2014 so 2 left unseen, and 2 discarded \u2192 total 4, ok.\n\nSimilarly, B6: unshown:3, no one discarded B6 \u2014 so 1 must be in my hand or meld.\n\nSame for B8.\n\nBut if I have B6 in hand AND in meld, that would require two B6 \u2014 possible only if I have a pair.\n\nBut I have B6:1 in hand \u2014 and one in meld \u2014 total two \u2014 ok, if I had a pair.\n\nBut when I used B6 in meld, I should have only one.\n\nUnless I had two B6.\n\nBut hand says B6:1 \u2014 so only one.\n\nConclusion: **the hand tiles list should NOT include B6,