ks both All Pungs and Full Flush (mixed suits).\n  - **Half Flush** (6 points): Possible if we go for Characters + Honors. We have W9, F4\u00d72, J2, and could aim for more W tiles. But only W9 currently \u2014 too weak.\n  - **Outside Hand** (4 points): Every meld includes terminals or honors. Current melds: [B6,B7,B8] \u2014 all simples (not terminals or honors) \u2192 invalidates Outside Hand.\n    - Therefore, **Outside Hand is impossible** due to middle chow.\n  - **All Simples** (2 points): Also broken by W9, F4, J2 \u2014 all non-simples.\n  - So our hand currently scores very low. Likely only eligible for minimal patterns unless improved.\n\nBut note: We have **[B5,B5,B5]** (exposed pung of terminal), and **[B6,B7,B8]** (middle chow), plus W9 (terminal), B9 (terminal), F4\u00d72 (honor), J2 (dragon).\n\nNo strong pattern emerging. Best strategy: minimize risk and consider safety.\n\nTile Danger Assessment:\n- **J2**: 4 unshown \u2014 many still out, risky to discard.\n- **F4**: 4 unshown \u2014 also common, but next player has no wind melds, across player hasn\u2019t shown interest. Still, North Wind isn\u2019t prevalent or seat wind \u2014 less valuable.\n- **B9**: Only 2 unshown (we hold 1, 3 seen/discarded?), actually: total 4 copies \u2014 unshown says B9:2 \u2192 so 2 remain unseen. Moderate danger.\n- **W9**: Unshown: 4 \u2192 all still available! That means no one has discarded or claimed W9 yet. Very dangerous \u2014 could complete someone\u2019s terminal/honor pung.\n\nWait \u2014 contradiction: \"Unshown tiles are: ... W9: 4\" \u2014 meaning all four W9s are still unclaimed? But we don\u2019t have any W9 in hand? Wait \u2014 yes we do: **Your hand tiles are: [W9: 1; ...]** \u2192 so one W9 in hand. Then unshown = 4 means **three other W9s still in play** \u2014 extremely dangerous.\n\nSo **discarding W9 is highly dangerous** \u2014 could feed a pung.\n\nSimilarly, **B9**: we have one, unshown: 2 \u2192 two others exist \u2014 still risky.\n\nBest d